1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,310
The Evomorph: something hid in the cargo from Titan-6, and now it's loose on the

2
00:00:04,310 --> 00:00:05,463
ship, and it's growing.

3
00:00:05,683 --> 00:00:06,963
Here's how it plays.

4
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:11,052
Put the Evolution card by the Killer board with its marker on Hatchling.

5
00:00:11,272 --> 00:00:15,752
Shuffle the Evomorph's and the location's Terror cards as normal, but use only eight

6
00:00:15,752 --> 00:00:20,072
cards, not ten. Shuffle the Ambush cards face down with the light green Youngling

7
00:00:20,072 --> 00:00:23,325
side readable. And the Evomorph starts with just four health.

8
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:27,653
The Evomorph has three stages: Hatchling, Youngling and Adult.

9
00:00:27,873 --> 00:00:31,679
The word EVOLVE appears twice in the effects column of its Bloodlust track.

10
00:00:31,679 --> 00:00:35,942
When Bloodlust rises onto an EVOLVE, move the Evolution marker to the next stage and

11
00:00:35,942 --> 00:00:37,921
apply that stage's rules straight away.

12
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:42,168
The Hatchling is slow but very deadly. Attack it at your own risk.

13
00:00:42,388 --> 00:00:45,771
Bloodlust only goes up when the Hatchling kills a Victim itself.

14
00:00:45,771 --> 00:00:49,999
Every other Bloodlust increase, from Terror cards, Events, or Victims dying some

15
00:00:49,999 --> 00:00:54,228
other way, is ignored. Instead, you lose one Time for each increase you ignored.

16
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:58,985
When it evolves into a Youngling, it immediately Vanishes, and from then on

17
00:00:58,985 --> 00:01:00,303
Bloodlust rises normally.

18
00:01:00,523 --> 00:01:05,068
When the Youngling evolves into an Adult, its maximum health goes from four to ten

19
00:01:05,068 --> 00:01:09,557
and it recovers all its health. Reveal its Dark Power card, and rotate the Ambush

20
00:01:09,557 --> 00:01:12,107
deck so the dark green Adult side is readable.

21
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:16,956
Whenever you see the Vanish icon, the Evomorph disappears into the shadows and the

22
00:01:16,956 --> 00:01:20,880
Killer phase ends. Take its meeple off the board and put it on top of the Terror

23
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:21,125
deck.

24
00:01:21,345 --> 00:01:24,842
While it has vanished, skip every normal step of the Killer phase:

25
00:01:24,842 --> 00:01:27,120
no Finale Killer Action and no Terror card.

26
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:30,881
Instead draw one Ambush card and follow the side for its current stage.

27
00:01:31,101 --> 00:01:33,688
Each side has a red Danger number from one to ten.

28
00:01:33,688 --> 00:01:36,067
The higher the number, the nastier the effect.

29
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:40,154
Many Ambush cards bring it back out of nowhere, often in your space, attacking.

30
00:01:40,154 --> 00:01:42,792
Reshuffle the Ambush discards if the deck runs out.

31
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,602
You get three new Scan Action cards, and they can only be played while the Evomorph

32
00:01:47,602 --> 00:01:48,229
has vanished.

33
00:01:48,449 --> 00:01:52,585
With two successes, place a Scan token in your space and lower Horror by one.

34
00:01:52,585 --> 00:01:55,539
With one success, place a Scan token and lose one Time.

35
00:01:55,539 --> 00:01:59,031
With none, your Horror rises, you lose a Time and your turn ends.

36
00:01:59,251 --> 00:02:03,777
A Scan token means you know it isn't hiding there, and many Ambush cards can't place

37
00:02:03,777 --> 00:02:06,632
it in a space with a Scan token. One token per space;

38
00:02:06,632 --> 00:02:08,680
if you run out, move the farthest one.

39
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:13,146
With three successes, you ambush it: place the Evomorph in your space, skip the next

40
00:02:13,146 --> 00:02:15,876
Killer phase, and remove that Scan card from the game.

41
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:19,341
Its Dark Power appears when it becomes an Adult.

42
00:02:19,341 --> 00:02:23,798
Each one places it in the closest space to you without a Scan token, then removes

43
00:02:23,798 --> 00:02:24,679
all Scan tokens.

44
00:02:24,899 --> 00:02:28,529
Razor Claws: whenever it damages you, discard a random Action card.

45
00:02:28,529 --> 00:02:32,323
Acid Blood: whenever you damage it in your space, you lose one health.

46
00:02:32,323 --> 00:02:36,658
Symbiotic Camouflage: draw an extra Ambush card and use the one with the highest

47
00:02:36,658 --> 00:02:37,037
Danger.

48
00:02:37,257 --> 00:02:41,716
Its Epic Dark Power, Razor Tail, kills every Victim in the most crowded unscanned

49
00:02:41,716 --> 00:02:45,513
space, and whenever it attacks, it also attacks every adjacent space.

50
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:50,963
Its Finales change its Killer Action. The Perfect Organism moves twice and attacks

51
00:02:50,963 --> 00:02:53,843
twice. Blitz of Death attacks two separate targets.

52
00:02:54,063 --> 00:02:58,120
Death in the Dark attacks and then Vanishes every Killer phase, drawing an extra

53
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,844
Ambush card and keeping the worst.

54
00:03:00,064 --> 00:03:04,879
And its Epic Finale, Impenetrable Armor, reduces all damage you deal it by two, to a

55
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:05,739
minimum of one.

56
00:03:06,567 --> 00:03:10,880
A few tips. Don't fight the Hatchling: keep Victims away from it so it can't evolve,

57
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,756
and the Time penalty is cheaper than a stronger monster.

58
00:03:13,976 --> 00:03:18,072
Hold your Scan cards for when it vanishes, and scan the space you plan to stand in.

59
00:03:18,292 --> 00:03:22,020
A three-success Scan drops it into your space with a skipped Killer phase:

60
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:24,287
the perfect moment to hit it hard. Good luck.

